   "text": "I read the structure region by region and wrote it as a maleimidocaproyl\u2011N\u2011methylvaline\u2011valine\u2011dolaisoleuine\u2011dolaproine\u2011phenylalanine chain, which is the mc\u2011MMAF framework.\n\n- **Left end:** a maleimide ring, N\u2011linked to a five\u2011carbon chain (CCCCC) that ends in an amide carbonyl on an N\u2011methyl nitrogen.\n- **First residue:** an N\u2011methylvaline. I checked its stereocentre against the wedge on the isopropyl group, and it comes out as `[C@H]` in the SMILES order used below.\n- **Second residue:** a valine joined through an NH.\n- **Next unit:** an N\u2011methylated carbon bearing a sec\u2011butyl group, then a CH(OMe) carbon and a CH2\u2013C(=O) group. This is the dolaisoleuine unit.\n- **Pyrrolidine unit:** the carbonyl is attached to the ring nitrogen. The ring carbon next to the nitrogen carries a CH(OMe)\u2013CH(CH3)\u2013C(=O) side chain. This is the dolaproine unit.\n- **C\u2011terminus:** an NH\u2011linked phenylalanine with a free COOH and a phenyl ring.\n\nI checked the first valine's centre directly from the drawing. For the other stereocentres I relied on the known MMAF configuration rather than re\u2011deriving each one from the wedges.\n\nSMILES: CC[C@H](C)[C@@H]([C@@H](CC(=O)N1CCC[C@H]1[C@H](OC)[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccccc1)C(O)=O)OC)N(C)C(=O)[C@@H](NC(=O)[C@H](C(C)C)N(C)C(=O)CCCCCN1C(=O)C=CC1=O)C(C)C"
